Your Committee has been planning the arrangements for the opening of our new premises at 28, rue des Acacias.  You will find below the social programme drawn up for the rest of 2009.  We hope you will be able to support these events.  These are exciting t
imes for our Branch.  Our Treasurer is gratefully receiving your subscriptions and this is my opportunity to thank you all for your continued support.  It is your Committee\rquote 
s firm belief that with our new premises we are now in good shape to present the RBL in the best possible light in order to attract new members.  To this end we have organized a Portes Ouvertes on Friday 4}{\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\super\langnp1033 th}{
\fs22\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033  December to welcome members of the wider Paris community in order to tell them about the RBL, our aims and our ambitions. On this oc
casion, in support of this strategy, Les Clack has offered to present a session of War Poetry Reading. A collection will take place afterwards in aid of the 2009 Poppy Appeal.  If you have friends who you believe would consider joining the RBL then do ple
ase invite them. 
\par Next week you will receive your  tickets for our Tombola to be held on Friday 18th December when the draw will take place at the Christmas Dinner. We look forward to your support.
\par }\pard \qc \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\nooverflow\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f63\fs28\lang1033\langfe1036\langnp1033 \'ab\~We will remenber them\~\'ab\~
